title: log-detail panel
tags: Panel [[Event log]]
kind: reference
aliases: log-detail snapshot before after diff selected_log_entry
summary: What a revision — or one operation of it — changed, field by field, following the log panel's cursor.

The [[log panel]] says ''that'' a revision happened; `log-detail` says what it did. Put
it in the other slot (`panel:open here log-detail`, <<key "panel:open here log-detail" "t e">>):
it follows the log panel's cursor (`selected_log_entry`) and reads the revision with its
snapshots.

* ''A revision'': its header — number, label, time, `HEAD` and `watcher` badges, operation count — then its operations, a hundred at a time (''Show more operations''): a reconcile is one revision of every file it found, never fetched whole.
* ''An operation'' (the cursor inside an expanded revision): that operation alone, highlighted; `log-detail:toggle whole` (the ''Whole revision'' button) widens to the revision.

Each operation shows its type, field and `undo of op N` badge, the metarecord it wrote with
that metarecord's ''current'' path — clicking the uuid selects it and shows it in the other
slot — and a before/after table: one row per field name, a name's values compared as a set
(fields are a multi-map), rows marked added, removed or changed. Fields the operation
recorded without changing are hidden, with a count, unless `log-detail:toggle unchanged`
(the ''Unchanged fields'' checkbox). A `tree_ref` value is shown as the path it names.

It re-reads when metarecords change (a rollback moves HEAD, a label may change);
`log-detail:refresh` does it by hand.
